This is the first major step towards autogenerating province mappings from triangulation point pairs. Splitting work into at least two pull requests because it's already quite a lot to review.

- The current PR doesn't implement the province mapping autogeneration. It only adds the reading, editing and saving of triangulation pairs.
- I haven't removed or modified the existing 3-pair triangulation feature yet. It may become obsolete when the persistent triangulation points are actually used for triangulation, which is not the case yet.
- The points are drawn on the canvas like the ones from the existing triangulation feature, except they are grey when inactive and blue for the currently selected pair.
- The pairs are displayed in a grid separate from the province mappings grid.
- The pairs can be added with the F6 key and removed with the Del key.

